  "prefLabel": "Lab 203.09 Consolidation",
  "recordType": "rule-section",
  "ruleText": "Lab 203.09 Consolidation. Where the interests of justice shall be better served without substantial prejudice to the rights of any party, the labor commissioner, the labor commissioner’s designee, or board as applicable shall sever one case from another or consolidate 2 or more cases preserving for all parties the right of appeal from the single or several decisions previously rendered.\n\nSource. #8922-A, eff 7-1-07; ss by #14534, eff 3-12-26 (formerly Lab 203.08)",
  "source": "https://github.com/GraniteState/adm-rules-data/blob/1c92d82e0f03a582ca5b7a578588edf38de2318e/raw/2026-11-15/state_agencies/lab200.html"
